    "result": "I implemented `shipping_cost` in `solution.py` and wrote a 110-case pytest suite in `tests/test_solution.py`. `python -m pytest -q tests` passes (110 passed). I could not run the coverage, CRAP, mutation or bandit gates here, so those are unverified. I reasoned through each branch and boundary by hand, and every function is small (cyclomatic complexity well under 10).\n\nThe implementation follows the spec. Weights are rounded up to the next 0.5 kg, the zone factor is applied to the base charge, free shipping and the oversize surcharge are applied as specified, and the total is quantized to two places with `ROUND_HALF_UP` at the end. Two choices go beyond the spec: NaN and infinite values raise `ValueError`, and the arithmetic runs in a local decimal context with 60-digit precision. The tests cover type and value errors, zone validation, all boundaries (150 subtotal, 120 cm, 0 subtotal, 0 dimensions), a half-up tie (15.625 → 15.63), and the float-through-`str()` conversion via `_to_decimal`, which the tests import directly.",
